description: 'Upgrade src/interface.rs from v1 flat IType header to interface.jhi
  v2: serialized typed HIR/MIR surface with generic signatures + HM constraints, value-semantics/borrow/as
  annotations, effect+capability rows, Perceus refcount obligations, enough for cross-.jnb
  inlining (docs/lamp-prereqs.md §3). Then the three-hash ladder: api hash (names+arity+nominal
  identities, warn-only), abi hash (RECURSIVE MERKLE CLOSURE over full transitive
  type/ownership/effect graph with cycle handling via SCC fixpoint: field layout/order/size,
  Perceus owned-vs-borrowed glue, cap/effect signature, calling-convention determinants),
  object hash (final object bytes, store keying + dedup + --verify). Used-surface
  hashing: abi hash for a dep edge is over only the subset the consumer''s MIR references
  (deterministic fold over the import set). Semantic hashes (api/abi) over canonical
  deterministic MIR; object hash over binary. Pin Merkle cycle algorithm so two compilers
  agree byte-for-byte. Blocked by 2-32-1 (Q2 per-target vs target-independent, Q9
  cross-toolchain stability) and 2-32-2 (effect rows) and 2-32-3 (identity in symbols).
  Definition of done: interface v2 round-trips, three hashes computed, used-surface
  fast-path test (minor bump keeps hash stable), conformance tests.'
